! strap2_chm102633945.strap -- CHM 102633945 (folder 03-02), "Annotated
! partial program listing", one page.  Read in the ink at 600 dpi,
! 2026-11-07.
!
! WHAT THIS PAGE IS.  A page of an assembler's own code, printed by a
! 7030 STRAP assembler.  Someone has annotated it in pencil for teaching:
! "Name", "Symbolic Instruction", "Comments", "Left Half", "Right Half",
! "Octal", "Hex", "Instruction Counter (Octal)".  The comments show what
! the code does.  It works out the size of a DR/DRZ reservation:
! "TEST FOR DR OR DRZ", "TEST IF PROD OF DIMEN *FL FORMED", "MULTIPLY
! BY PROD OF DIMEN", "FIELD LENGTH OF 64", "TRY TO GET L VALUE".  The
! ZI.../ZO... fields indexed by $3 and $5 are entries of the symbol and
! statement units.  docs/reconstruction_plan.md S-1 takes it as the only
! surviving lines of STRAP II.  The page carries no title, date or
! version, but C22-6729 (the STRAP II Systems Analysis Guide), read in
! the ink 2026-11-08, identifies it:
!   - printed p.27: in Pass 2, MQR's DR processing keeps "the location
!     of the basic portion of the vle dimension entry in the unit ... in
!     Ziotpt"; "When the final product is available ... it is put as a
!     negative number into the value field of Ziotpt"; "The Zifall
!     indicator is turned off to indicate to Pass 2 that there are coded
!     expressions ... not yet evaluated"; a null dds is (N,64,4).  Here:
!     LX,$9,ZIOTPT -DIMENSION REF ADDR; STN ... ZIOTPT -STORE NEGATIVE;
!     CM0000,ZIFALL -TURN OFF IND after -CANT FORM PROD; -FIELD LENGTH
!     OF 64.  p.12: the current unit's address is in $3 in Pass 2.
!   - printed p.96, Chart CB "STRAP II" MIOD, boxes 14 and 19: TURN
!     OFF / TURN ON ZIFALL INDICATOR.
!   - printed p.189, Figure 20, the unit's fixed format: ZIFFLF bit 27
!     and ZIFBSF bit 29 of the ZILCFD word, ZIFALL bit 25 and ZINFLD
!     bits 32-49 ("Number of Fields") of the ZILPMS word, ZIDDS from bit
!     50.  The page's values (1.33, 1.35, 2.31, 2.40(BU,18), DDS fields
!     at 2.65 and 2.73) agree bit for bit with ZIADAB as word 0.
!   - printed p.191, Figure 22: an evaluated dimension entry's
!     evaluation indicator follows a 20-bit header and a 5-bit field,
!     i.e. bit 5 of the basic portion: the page's BB,.05($9).
!   >>> ONE DISAGREEMENT, NOT SETTLED: Figure 20's rows put ZIOTPT in
!   word 5 (after ZICDID and ZIOPX); this page addresses it as word 4
!   (4.00).  Either the page predates a word of the unit, or the
!   figure's rows are not in word order.  (p.184's added word, ZICOMM,
!   is the LAST fixed word, so it is not the explanation.) <<<
!
! WHAT IS NOT ON THE PAGE, AND IS GIVEN HERE BY SYN.  The symbols the
! page uses but does not define: KZ, MORVAL and KEAA (branch targets),
! and the unit fields.  Each value below is read from the machine code
! the page prints for it, NOT from any other source.  A field's data
! description (BU,n) is read from the length its plain L prints; the
! one-bit fields are the targets of BZB:
!     KZ 201.0 (B,KZ prints 201.10 00), MORVAL 65.0, KEAA 160.0;
!     ZIFBSF 1.35, ZIFFLF 1.33, ZIFALL 2.31, ZODR 0.54, ZOEXT 0.57;
!     ZIDDSB 2.73 (BU,4), ZIDDSF 2.65 (BU,6), ZINFLD 2.40 (BU,18),
!     ZIOTPT 4.00 (BU,24).
! So the rows check the assembler's ENCODING of each operation and each
! modifier (BZB, BRZ, BXVLZ, BB, LX, SIC, *, ST, STN(B,...), CM0000,
! negative offsets), not the field values, which come from the page.
!
! THE LISTING'S OWN FORM, kept for the reconstruction:
!   - two columns for each instruction: the left half-word in octal W.B
!     and its last byte in hex, then the right half-word the same way.
!     Leading zeros of the left half are suppressed ("2.65 83").  The
!     third column is the location.
!   - "CV" follows the location on four lines, 000256.00, 000257.00,
!     000274.00 and 000275.00.  These are exactly the four statements
!     with a NEGATIVE offset (-18, -24, -24, -30).  That is what the
!     marks coincide with; their meaning is not read anywhere.
!   - "*" follows 000265.00 (B,MORVAL), and that statement's text is
!     set further right than its neighbours.  Meaning not established.
!     Compare the "*" after some locations on C22-6678-1 p.48
!     (decks/mcpref_example2.strap).
!   - the page's first statement is cut at the top.  The last line,
!     000277.40 "LI(B?,7),7  -TRY TO GET L VALUE", is too faint to
!     transcribe and is left as a comment.
!
! INK READINGS THAT NEEDED 600 DPI.
!   - 000250.40 B,KFNA: the third digit of 25?.10 is faint and lies
!     under the pencilled "Octal"; it reads 2 or 3.  The page's own
!     location column puts KFNA at 000253.00, so it is 3.
!   - 000254.40: the last byte is D0, the same as 000257.00's ST.  It
!     looks like 50 at 220 dpi.
!   - STN(B,25) is printed with mode B, not BU, at 000271.00 and
!     000275.00.  The code (.10, not .30) confirms it.

        SLC, (8)246.40
KZ      SYN, (8)201.0
MORVAL  SYN, (8)65.0
KEAA    SYN, (8)160.0
ZIFBSF  SYN(BU,1), (8)1.35
ZIDDSB  SYN(BU,4), (8)2.73
ZIFFLF  SYN(BU,1), (8)1.33
ZIDDSF  SYN(BU,6), (8)2.65
ZINFLD  SYN(BU,18), (8)2.40
ZIOTPT  SYN(BU,24), (8)4.00
ZODR    SYN(BU,1), (8)0.54
ZIFALL  SYN(BU,1), (8)2.31
ZOEXT   SYN(BU,1), (8)0.57
        BZB,ZIFBSF($3),KZ              ! TEST IF BYTE SIZE FILLED
        L,ZIDDSB($3)
        B,KFNA
KFN     BZB,ZIFFLF($3),KZ              ! TEST IF FL FILLED
        L,ZIDDSF($3)                   ! LOAD FL
KFNA    BRZ,KF1                        ! TEST FOR FL OF 64
        *(BU,18),ZINFLD($3)            ! FORM PROD
        ST(BU,24),ZIOTPT($3),20
        B,KZ
KF1     L,ZINFLD($3),-18               ! FIELD LENGTH OF 64
        ST(BU,24),ZIOTPT($3),-24
        B,KZ
KFA     BZB,ZODR($5),KFP               ! TEST FOR DR OR DRZ
        LX,$9,ZIOTPT($3)               ! DIMENSION REF ADDR
        BXVLZ,KZ                       ! TEST IF PROD OF DIMEN *FL FORMED
        BB,.05($9),KFA1                ! ZIOTPT HAS DIMEN REF ADDR TEST IF PRO
        L(BU,24),$9                    ! DIM REF ADDR IN LO-ORDER OF SR
        SIC,$15
        B,MORVAL
        LX,$9,ZIOTPT($3)               ! RESTORE$9  PROD COMPLETE EXIT
        B,KFA2                         ! CANT FORM PROD OF DIMENSIONS
KFA1    L,ZIDDSF($3)                   ! DIMEN PROD COMPLETE-LOAD FL
        BRZ,KFA3                       ! TEST FOR FL OF 64
        *(BU,24),.06($9)               ! MULTIPLY BY PROD OF DIMEN
        STN(B,25),ZIOTPT($3),20        ! STORE NEGATIVE
        B,KZ
KFA2    CM0000,ZIFALL($3)              ! TUN OFF IND
        B,KZ
KFA3    L(BU,24),.06($9),-24           ! LOAD DIMEN +BCD
        STN(B,25),ZIOTPT($3),-30       ! ADD 6 LO ORDER ZEROS FOR *64 ST
        B,KZ
KFP     BZB,ZOEXT($5),KEAA             ! TEST IF EXT- NORMAL INSERTION
!       LI(B?,7),7                     ! TRY TO GET L VALUE  (000277.40, too faint)
